<title>USA: Canadian Natural sees rising '97 cash flow.</title>
<headline>Canadian Natural sees rising '97 cash flow.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Natural Resources Ltd expects 1997 cash flow of C$5.61 per share, Chief Operating Officer Keith MacPhail told a conference Thursday.</p>
<p>He said cash flow per barrel of oil equivalent would rise to C$20.90 from C$19.82 in 1996.</p>
<p>Barrels of oil equivalent are calculated by dividing billions of cubic feet of natural gas by six and adding it to million barrels of crude and natural gas liquids.</p>
</text>
